+/** Keyset pagination over `(created_at, id)` - the same pair the composite index in
+ * `migrations/0004_claims_created_at_id_idx.sql` covers, in the same order. `$2`/`$3` are the
+ * cursor's half of the tiebreak and may be null for the first page; when they are not null,
+ * only rows strictly after that position are returned, so a row already handed to a caller
+ * can never be handed to them again no matter what gets inserted in the meantime. */
+export const LIST_CLAIMS_KEYSET =
+  "SELECT * FROM claims WHERE tenant_id = $1" +
+  " AND ($2::timestamptz IS NULL OR (created_at, id) > ($2, $3))" +
+  " ORDER BY created_at, id LIMIT $4"
 
 /** Used by the reconciliation job, which only ever has the insurer's own reference number
  * to go on. */
